  "slug": "great-arrow-digital",
  "name": "Great Arrow Digital",
  "url": "https://www.greatarrow.ai/api/mcp",
  "description": "Great Arrow Digital gives Claude a persistent, private memory of your work — shared with every other AI tool you use. Connect once and Claude can search your workspace memory, your synced documents (Google Drive, Notion, GitHub, Slack, Gmail, and more), your meetings, and your kanban board — and save new decisions, notes, and tasks back to the same place.\n\nEverything is scoped to private workspaces you control: each connection is approved on an explicit consent screen, every tool call is permission-gated by OAuth scopes, and you can revoke access at any time from your Connected apps page. Memories stay fresh automatically — recency-aware retrieval, source citations with links back to the original document, and integration syncs that keep knowledge current.\n\nSaving a conversation: if you ask Claude to save a chat or a handoff checkpoint, the messages and summary are sent to Great Arrow and stored in your workspace, so your next session — in Claude or any other assistant — can pick up where you left off. This only happens when you ask for it. You can read, export, or delete anything that was saved under Library → Conversations, and deleting a conversation deletes its stored messages.\n\nTypical day with Great Arrow connected: ask Claude \"what do we know about the Q3 launch?\" and get grounded answers with citations; say \"remember this decision\" and it's saved, tagged, and available to your other AI assistants; ask \"what changed this week?\" and get a digest of new memories, synced docs, and meetings.",
